websocat: failures exit non-zero, log lines go to stderr (homescoop#696, #1023, #868)

- A listener (listen_tcp, udp_server) that can't bind its address exits 15
  (EXIT_CODE_LISTEN_FAIL), and a readfile:/writefile:/appendfile: that
  can't open its file exits 16 (EXIT_CODE_FILE_OPEN_FAIL). Upstream v4
  logged them and exited 0, unlike its connect (14), lookup (20/21) and
  TLS (8) failures.
- tracing's log lines go to stderr; upstream's fmt::init() wrote them to
  stdout, into the data a pipe or redirect carries.

Upstream: not filed (Lars decides).

--- a/src/main.rs
+++ b/src/main.rs
@@ -12,7 +12,8 @@
     }
     #[cfg(not(feature = "tokioconsole"))]
     {
-        tracing_subscriber::fmt::init();
+        // Log lines go to stderr, not into the data on stdout (homescoop#868).
+        tracing_subscriber::fmt().with_writer(std::io::stderr).init();
     }
     let argv = std::env::args_os();
     let stderr = std::io::stderr();
